# Breaking changes to the standard library's public surface, declared.
#
# `scripts/check-compat.sh` refuses a removed, retyped or
# effect-widened public name unless a line here names it against the
# version that makes the change. That is the whole enforcement: a
# break is allowed, and it is allowed only when somebody wrote down
# that they meant it.
#
# Format, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <version>  <kind-letter>  <name>  <why>
#
# The kind letter is AXSYM's: F function, D data, C constructor,
# S struct, T trait. `docs/compatibility.md` is the policy this file
# implements.

# 0.3.3 - ERR-ADOPT-1 slice 3, the half of it where `-errno` genuinely
# means a failure. Seven filesystem calls and `copyFile` answer
# `(Result Int Error)` instead of an Int that is a byte count when
# positive and a negated errno when negative. See docs/error-model.md
# section 10.
0.3.3  F  writeFile   -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  appendFile  -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  removeFile  -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  renamePath  -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  fileSize    -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  makeDirAll  -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  removeDir   -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
0.3.3  F  copyFile    -errno -> (Result Int Error): the failure is in the type
